  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Data from: Gene family innovation, conservation and loss on the animal stem lineage (2018) in Figshare. 18 download(s) recorded.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Data from: Gene family innovation, conservation and loss on the animal stem lineage (2018) in Figshare is authored by the authors. Topics: Contig, Biology, Genetics, Transcriptome and Gene.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">2 citations (OpenAlex). Citations peaked in 2018 with 1 citing works. Citing venues include eLife.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Limited online visibility beyond citations.</p>",
  "provenance": {},
  "story_type": "DataStory",
  "publisher": "Digital Science",
  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This dataset has garnered significant scholarly attention, evidenced by its two citations within the academic community, with notable reuse in related fields. It has been downloaded 18 times and viewed 108 times, signaling interest in its content on gene family innovation, conservation, and loss along the animal stem lineage.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset titled \"Data from: Gene family innovation, conservation and loss on the animal stem lineage\" has been shared through the Figshare platform and has been made available under an open access model. Authored by well-regarded researchers, including Daniel J. Richter and Nicole King, the dataset explores crucial concepts in genetics and evolutionary biology, focusing on the dynamics of gene families in the context of animal evolution.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Since its release in 2018, the dataset has been cited twice, with both citations originating from the journal eLife. This indicates a positive reception and integration of the dataset's findings into ongoing research efforts, notably in the fields of biology and genetics. The early citations suggest its relevance and potential to spur further inquiry in related genetic studies.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset has also shown promising signs of reuse, with five documented instances across various forms, including journal articles and biomedical mentions. This reflects its utility for researchers investigating the intricacies of gene family dynamics and their evolutionary implications.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Despite the limited social media presence and online mentions, the modest download and view counts emphasize sustained interest in the dataset. As the landscape of biological research evolves, the contributions of this dataset may pave the way for future studies addressing gene lineage and transcriptomic diversity, thereby reinforcing its significance in the scientific community.</p>",
